### Detailed Solution

y = f(x) \Rightarrow \frac{dy}{dx} = f'(x)
\left(\frac{dy}{dx}\right)_{(1,f(1))} = f'(1) = \tan \frac{\pi}{6} = \frac{1}{\sqrt{3}}
\left(\frac{dy}{dx}\right)_{(3,f(3))} = f'(3) = \tan \frac{\pi}{4} = 1
\text{We need to evaluate } 27\int_{1}^{3} ((f'(t))^2 + 1)f''(t)dt = \alpha + \beta\sqrt{3}
\text{Let } I = \int_{1}^{3} ((f'(t))^2 + 1)f''(t)dt
\text{Substitute } f'(t) = z \Rightarrow f''(t)dt = dz
\text{Change limits:}
\text{When } t=3, z = f'(3) = 1
\text{When } t=1, z = f'(1) = \frac{1}{\sqrt{3}}
I = \int_{1/\sqrt{3}}^{1} (z^2 + 1)dz
= \left[\frac{z^3}{3} + z\right]_{1/\sqrt{3}}^{1}
= \left(\frac{1^3}{3} + 1\right) - \left(\frac{(1/\sqrt{3})^3}{3} + \frac{1}{\sqrt{3}}\right)
= \left(\frac{1}{3} + 1\right) - \left(\frac{1}{3 \cdot 3\sqrt{3}} + \frac{1}{\sqrt{3}}\right)
= \frac{4}{3} - \left(\frac{1}{9\sqrt{3}} + \frac{1}{\sqrt{3}}\right)
= \frac{4}{3} - \left(\frac{1}{9\sqrt{3}} + \frac{9}{9\sqrt{3}}\right)
= \frac{4}{3} - \frac{10}{9\sqrt{3}}
= \frac{4}{3} - \frac{10\sqrt{3}}{27}
\text{Now, substitute this back into the original expression:}
\alpha + \beta\sqrt{3} = 27 \left(\frac{4}{3} - \frac{10\sqrt{3}}{27}\right)
= 27 \times \frac{4}{3} - 27 \times \frac{10\sqrt{3}}{27}
= 9 \times 4 - 10\sqrt{3}
= 36 - 10\sqrt{3}
\text{Comparing } \alpha + \beta\sqrt{3} \text{ with } 36 - 10\sqrt{3}, \text{ we get:}
\alpha = 36
\beta = -10
\text{The value of } \alpha + \beta \text{ is:}
\alpha + \beta = 36 + (-10) = 26

